Spec: Secure usable stream verification

Purpose:
  Verify device identity, publisher-enforced grants and actual independent application data transfer.

Owns:
  ./SecureStreamTests.cs

References:
  /examples/secure-direct/secure-direct.sdd

Must:
  Reject wrong roots, keys, devices, applications, services and absent/revoked grants before business delivery.
  Cover partial IO, one-use tickets, blocked-IO revocation, identity binding, retained opens and restart recovery locally.
  Use the referenced independent application verifier for large authenticated HTTPS, WebSocket, half-close and consumer dependency checks.
  Distinguish local two-Agent verification from unexecuted physical multi-device or NAT traversal tests.
  Verify an explicit per-service peer listener refuses a different otherwise authorized service and that retained relay outcomes survive restart without path relabeling.

  An experimental open with unsupported declared relay limits fails before any peer connection.
